From b92f05c5661c6171b6dc42e4eef25adeb00aa91f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Medium1992 <122653016+Medium1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:29:34 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] XHTTP client: Grow the HTTP/2 downlink window with the
 reader

A node that dials XHTTP over HTTP/2, such as a transit hop, buffers up
to its 4 MiB stream window of downlink data whenever the local reader
falls behind. The same flow governor now wraps the connections the
HTTP/2 transport dials, in a client role that governs only the
downlink: the server is shown the 64 KiB initial window and gets the
transport's credit back only while unread data stays under twice what
the reader consumed over the lowest recent round trip, measured with
PING towards the server.

The uplink is left to the server, which buffers it. Any server works
unchanged, stock or governed.
